Here's the formal **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of your integration test suite, with integration-test calibration applied (class is marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`).

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4**          |

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ← blocks for 3 seconds unconditionally
```

**Integration calibration:** Even for integration tests, a hard sleep is a smell — it introduces flakiness (may be too short on CI, always too long locally) and inflates suite runtime.

**Fix:**
```csharp
// Poll with timeout instead
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(100, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky CI failures; suite slowdown scales linearly with test count.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Problem:** One branch will *never* execute — either the user is always premium or never is. The untested path creates hidden coverage gaps.

**Fix:** Split into two deterministic tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsBasicProperties()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscountRate()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("prem@example.com", "Prem", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("prem@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — a dead branch is never caught by CI.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertion — passes even if Insert silently discards data
}
```

**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Test provides zero bug-detection value — it passes even if every insert is a no-op.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` | **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

4 assertions, none with a failure message. When one fails in CI, the stack trace shows only a line number — you must read the source to determine *what* property was wrong.

**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower triage time when failures occur in CI logs.

---

## ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Designed Tests)

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused assertions |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single behavior, single assertion, obvious |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count after 3 inserts is self-documenting (not Magic Number) |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, clear verification |

The fixture setup (in-memory SQLite) is compact and used by all tests — **no General Fixture smell**.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | 2 min | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | 10 min | Split into two deterministic tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | 10 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling loop |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | 5 min | Add message strings to `InsertUser` assertions |

Items 1–3 prevent **false-pass scenarios** and should be fixed before merging. Item 4 is a diagnostic-quality improvement for triage speed.
